---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Insights & News - DecAltra"
  description="Perspectives on credit decision infrastructure, research, and updates from DecAltra."
>
  <div class="insights-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <section class="intro" aria-labelledby="page-title">
        <div class="kicker">Ideas and updates from DecAltra</div>
        <h1 id="page-title">Insights &amp; News</h1>
      </section>
      <section aria-label="Insights and news" class="perspective-grid">
        <article class="perspective-tile">
          <div class="tile-top">
            <span class="tag">Decision infrastructure</span><span
              >Perspective</span
            >
          </div>
          <h2>
            <button data-open="perspective">
              Better credit infrastructure.<br />Better economics of lending.
            </button>
          </h2>
          <p class="tile-deck">
            The work required to assess and monitor a borrower shapes the
            economics of providing credit. DecAltra exists to make that work
            more efficient, connected, and traceable.
          </p>

          <figure class="research-quote card-quote">
            <blockquote>
              &ldquo;Taking steps to lower delivery and monitoring costs would
              be instrumental in improving the economics of SME lending.&rdquo;
            </blockquote>
            <figcaption>
              <a
                href="https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/bank-insights/2026/what-drives-differences-in-commercial-banks-product-level-returns"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                >Manning et al. · Bank of England · 2026 ↗</a
              >
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="takeaways">
            <h3>Main takeaways</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>
                Delivery and monitoring costs are part of the SME lending
                challenge.
              </li>
              <li>
                Digitalisation can improve credit preparation, assessment, and
                oversight.
              </li>
              <li>
                Our ambition: less repeated work, connected evidence, and
                professionals in control.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="tile-sources">
            <h3>Research informing our perspective</h3>
            <a
              href="https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/bank-insights/2026/what-drives-differences-in-commercial-banks-product-level-returns"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >Bank of England · Lending economics · 2026 ↗</a
            ><a
              href="https://www.bancaditalia.it/pubblicazioni/temi-discussione/2023/2023-1406/index.html?com.dotmarketing.htmlpage.language=1"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >Banca d&#8217;Italia · Technology adoption and lending · 2023 ↗</a
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tile-bottom">
            <button class="note-button" data-open="perspective">
              Read perspective ↗</button
            ><span>DecAltra perspective</span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="perspective-tile">
          <div class="tile-top">
            <span class="tag">Private credit &amp; operations</span><span
              >Perspective</span
            >
          </div>
          <h2>
            <button data-open="private-credit">
              Growing private credit needs stronger infrastructure.
            </button>
          </h2>
          <p class="tile-deck">
            Private credit is financing businesses that require a detailed
            understanding of cash flows, business models and risk. Drawing on
            BIS and industry research, we explore why connected underwriting,
            monitoring and reporting matter as portfolios grow.
          </p>
          <figure class="research-quote card-quote">
            <blockquote>
              &ldquo;…introducing greater efficiencies into the lending process
              with the help of new technology…&rdquo;
            </blockquote>
            <figcaption>
              <a
                href="https://acc.aima.org/research/financing-the-economy.html"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                >ACC / AIMA &amp; Dechert · The Future of Private Credit ↗</a
              >
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="takeaways">
            <h3>Main takeaways</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>
                Investors expect strong risk management, monitoring, and
                reporting.
              </li>
              <li>
                BIS research highlights the role of cash flows and intangible
                assets in private-credit lending.
              </li>
              <li>
                Our view: information should stay connected from assessment into
                ongoing oversight.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="tile-sources">
            <h3>Research informing our perspective</h3><a
              href="https://www.bis.org/publications/qr-202609/financing-digital-economy-role-private-credit"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >BIS · Financing the digital economy · 2026 ↗</a
            >
            <a
              href="https://acc.aima.org/research/financing-the-economy.html"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >ACC / AIMA · The Future of Private Credit ↗</a
            ><a
              href="https://acc.aima.org/education-acc/acc-financing-the-economy.html"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >ACC / AIMA · Financing the Economy series ↗</a
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tile-bottom">
            <button class="note-button" data-open="private-credit">
              Read perspective ↗</button
            ><span>DecAltra perspective</span>
          </div>
        </article>
      </section>
      <section class="manifesto">
        <div>
          <div class="kicker">From perspective to practice</div>
          <h2>Better decisions start<br />with better foundations.</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>
            DecAltra connects information, analysis, and professional judgement.
            Our ambition is to help financial institutions spend less time
            preparing a case and more time understanding the opportunity in
            front of them.
          </p>
          <a class="textlink" href="/credit-decisioning"
            >Explore Credit Decisioning <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
          >
        </div>
      </section>
    </div><dialog id="perspective" aria-labelledby="perspective-title">
      <div class="dialog-bar">
        <span>DecAltra perspective · Decision infrastructure</span><button
          class="close"
          aria-label="Close perspective">×</button
        >
      </div>
      <article class="article">
        <h2 id="perspective-title">
          Better credit infrastructure. Better economics of lending.
        </h2>
        <p>
          DecAltra starts with a conviction: the infrastructure behind financial
          decisions deserves attention alongside the availability of capital
          itself.
        </p>
        <h3>The economic problem</h3>
        <p>
          Financing frictions can interrupt investment and expansion. The Bank
          of England’s discussion of
          <a
            href="https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/bank-insights/2026/finance-growth-and-productive-investment-what-is-the-fpc-assessing-in-2026"
            >finance and productive investment</a
          >
          emphasises the importance of suitable finance, alongside resilience.
        </p>
        <figure class="research-quote">
          <blockquote>
            &ldquo;Taking steps to lower delivery and monitoring costs would be
            instrumental in improving the economics of SME lending. SME loans
            are typically smaller, more heterogeneous and more labour‑intensive
            to assess, which raises operating costs per‑loan and depresses
            returns. Investment in digitalisation, automation and data‑driven
            credit processes can materially reduce these costs by streamlining
            underwriting, improving risk assessment, and enabling more efficient
            ongoing monitoring.&rdquo;
          </blockquote>
          <figcaption>
            Manning, Babu, Bourdais &amp; Włodarski · Bank of England · 19 June
            2026<br /><a
              href="https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/bank-insights/2026/what-drives-differences-in-commercial-banks-product-level-returns"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >What drives differences in commercial banks&#8217; product level
              returns? ↗</a
            >
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <h3>Lower costs, stronger decision infrastructure</h3>
        <p>
          The Bank’s
          <a
            href="https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/bank-insights/2026/what-drives-differences-in-commercial-banks-product-level-returns"
            >analysis of lending returns</a
          >
          identifies operating costs as one contributor to lower SME lending profitability.
          Its estimates depend on cost-allocation assumptions and do not describe
          every bank’s experience.
        </p>
        <p>
          Banca d&#8217;Italia&#8217;s study of lending during the pandemic
          found that more digitalised banks expanded credit more, particularly
          to smaller, financially sounder firms. Its crisis setting matters; we
          see it as supporting context for the role of technology in lending
          capacity.
        </p>
        <h3>The information problem</h3>
        <p>
          The
          <a
            href="https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/bank-overground/2025/unlocking-growth-what-can-the-literature-tell-us-about-whats-holding-back-high-growth-firms"
            >review of high-growth firms</a
          >
          highlights the role of information and relationships in financing. Understanding
          a business involves context as well as numbers.
        </p>
        <h3>Why we are building Credit Decisioning Infrastructure</h3>
        <p>
          Our reading is that the work required to deliver and monitor credit is
          an economic constraint worth addressing. This is central to
          DecAltra&#8217;s reason for existing.
        </p>
        <p>
          DecAltra&#8217;s Credit Decisioning Infrastructure is designed to
          connect financial spreading, analysis, credit memoranda, and portfolio
          oversight. Our aim is to reduce repeated preparation and fragmented
          handovers while preserving the evidence behind each decision.
        </p>
        <p>
          For credit teams, that means a workflow built around three priorities:
        </p>
        <ul class="references">
          <li>
            <strong>Less repeated work:</strong> carry information and analysis through
            the assessment process.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Clearer review:</strong> keep sources, adjustments, and assumptions
            connected to the conclusions professionals assess.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Continuity into monitoring:</strong> connect the assessment of
            a borrower with the portfolio view and the next action.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Our vision</h3>
        <p>
          We want to help financial institutions make sound credit decisions
          more efficiently, so that the cost of understanding and monitoring a
          business becomes less of a barrier to serving it.
        </p>
        <blockquote>
          Help suitable capital reach productive opportunities sooner.
        </blockquote>
        <p>
          The research strengthens the economic rationale for this ambition. The
          outcomes of using DecAltra must be established in practice, through
          measures such as preparation time, review effort, and monitoring
          workload.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/credit-decisioning"
            >Explore DecAltra&#8217;s Credit Decisioning Infrastructure ↗</a
          >
        </p>
        <p class="small editorial-note">
          Written by DecAltra, drawing on the research referenced below.
          Interpretations and conclusions are our own.
        </p>
        <h3>Research references</h3>
        <ol class="references">
          <li>
            Colm Manning, Prashant Babu, Ben Bourdais and Robert Włodarski.
            <a
              href="https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/bank-insights/2026/what-drives-differences-in-commercial-banks-product-level-returns"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >What drives differences in commercial banks&#8217; product level
              returns?</a
            >
            Bank of England, Bank Insights, 19 June 2026.
          </li>
          <li>
            Sarah Breeden and Colm Manning.
            <a
              href="https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/bank-insights/2026/finance-growth-and-productive-investment-what-is-the-fpc-assessing-in-2026"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >Finance, growth and productive investment: what is the FPC
              assessing in 2026?</a
            >
            Bank of England, Bank Insights, 22 September 2026.
          </li>
          <li>
            Bank of England.
            <a
              href="https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/bank-overground/2025/unlocking-growth-what-can-the-literature-tell-us-about-whats-holding-back-high-growth-firms"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >Unlocking growth: what can the literature tell us about
              what&#8217;s holding back high-growth firms?</a
            >
            Bank Overground, 2 October 2025. Prepared with the help of Sudipto Karmakar
            and Isabelle Roland.
          </li>
          <li>
            Nicola Branzoli, Edoardo Rainone and Ilaria Supino.
            <a
              href="https://www.bancaditalia.it/pubblicazioni/temi-discussione/2023/2023-1406/index.html?com.dotmarketing.htmlpage.language=1"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >The role of banks&#8217; technology adoption in credit markets
              during the pandemic.</a
            >
            Banca d&#8217;Italia, Working Paper 1406, March 2023.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </article>
    </dialog>
    <dialog id="private-credit" aria-labelledby="private-credit-title">
      <div class="dialog-bar">
        <span>DecAltra perspective · Private credit</span><button
          class="close"
          aria-label="Close perspective">×</button
        >
      </div>
      <article class="article">
        <h2 id="private-credit-title">
          Growing private credit needs stronger infrastructure.
        </h2>
        <p>
          For a credit manager, growth brings more than additional lending
          opportunities. It brings more cases to assess, borrowers to monitor,
          and decisions to explain.
        </p>
        <h3>Operating expectations grow with capital</h3>
        <p>
          The Alternative Credit Council&#8217;s industry research describes
          investor expectations around risk management, portfolio monitoring,
          and reporting as drivers of investment in operating infrastructure. It
          also identifies new technology as a means of improving lending
          efficiency.
        </p>
        <h3>The businesses being financed are evolving</h3>
        <p>
          BIS research on US direct lending from 2010 to 2025 describes how
          private credit met rising demand from software and technology firms,
          lending against recurring revenues and intangible assets. It also
          identifies narrowing spreads alongside a shift towards borrowers with
          weaker fundamentals, raising questions about risk pricing.
        </p>
        <p>
          For us, this reinforces the importance of understanding a borrower's
          business model and carrying underwriting assumptions into monitoring.
          The evidence is US-focused; it does not establish the outcomes of
          using decision infrastructure.
        </p>
        <h3>Connect the life of a credit</h3>
        <p>
          Our perspective is that information should remain usable after the
          initial approval. The assumptions behind underwriting should inform
          monitoring, and portfolio observations should help teams identify what
          needs attention next.
        </p>
        <h3>What this means for DecAltra</h3>
        <p>
          We aim to connect financial analysis, credit memoranda, and portfolio
          oversight so that teams can carry knowledge forward. Our ambition is
          to reduce repeated preparation and make the evidence behind a decision
          easier to review as the portfolio develops.
        </p>
        <blockquote>
          Carry the understanding forward, from underwriting to oversight.
        </blockquote>
        <p class="small editorial-note">
          Written by DecAltra, drawing on the research referenced below.
          Interpretations and conclusions are our own. Sources include BIS
          analysis of US direct lending and industry research based on manager
          interviews and survey evidence.
        </p>
        <h3>Research references</h3>
        <ol class="references">
          <li>
            Bank for International Settlements.
            <a
              href="https://www.bis.org/publications/qr-202609/financing-digital-economy-role-private-credit"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >Financing the digital economy: the role of private credit.</a
            >
            BIS Quarterly Review, 14 September 2026. Analysis of US direct lending,
            2010–2025.
          </li>
          <li>
            Alternative Credit Council / AIMA and Dechert.
            <a
              href="https://acc.aima.org/research/financing-the-economy.html"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >Financing the Economy — The Future of Private Credit.</a
            >
            Industry research on the development and operating needs of private credit.
          </li>
          <li>
            Alternative Credit Council / AIMA.
            <a
              href="https://acc.aima.org/education-acc/acc-financing-the-economy.html"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >Financing the Economy research series.</a
            >
            Further market context, including the 2024 and 2025 editions.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </article>
    </dialog>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script>
  const root = document.querySelector('.insights-page');
  root?.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-open]').forEach(button => {
    button.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const dialog = root.querySelector<HTMLDialogElement>(
        '#' + button.dataset.open
      );
      dialog?.showModal();
    });
  });
  root?.querySelectorAll<HTMLDialogElement>('dialog').forEach(dialog => {
    dialog
      .querySelector('.close')
      ?.addEventListener('click', () => dialog.close());
    dialog.addEventListener('click', event => {
      if (event.target !== dialog) return;
      const rect = dialog.getBoundingClientRect();
      if (
        event.clientX < rect.left ||
        event.clientX > rect.right ||
        event.clientY < rect.top ||
        event.clientY > rect.bottom
      )
        dialog.close();
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  .insights-page {
    --ink: #17201d;
    --muted: #626f69;
    --line: #d8e0db;
    --green: #496d58;
    --display: 'Mona Sans', sans-serif;
    color: var(--ink);
    font:
      15px/1.65 Inter,
      sans-serif;
  }
  * {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }
  a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  button {
    font: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  a:focus-visible,
  button:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid #629478;
    outline-offset: 5px;
  }
  h1,
  h2,
  h3,
  p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  h1,
  h2,
  h3 {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }
  .wrap {
    max-width: 1280px;
    margin: auto;
    padding: 0 40px;
  }
  .intro {
    padding: 57px 0 39px;
  }
  .kicker {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 9px;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 28px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-mist-700);
  }
  .kicker::before {
    content: '';
    width: 5px;
    height: 5px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: currentColor;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(36px, 4.6vw, 60px);
    margin: 17px 0 20px;
  }
  .perspective-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 26px;
    margin-top: 44px;
    align-items: stretch;
  }
  .perspective-tile {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-rows: subgrid;
    grid-row: span 7;
    row-gap: 0;
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 34px;
    transition:
      box-shadow 0.2s,
      border-color 0.2s;
  }
  .perspective-tile:hover {
    border-color: #9aad9b;
    box-shadow: 0 12px 30px #243a2e0b;
  }
  .tile-top {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    color: var(--color-mist-700);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 24px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .tag {
    color: #52725d;
    background: #edf3ed;
    padding: 4px 10px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .perspective-tile h2 {
    font-size: 34px;
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin: 26px 0 18px;
  }
  .perspective-tile h2 button {
    text-align: left;
    font: inherit;
    letter-spacing: inherit;
    color: inherit;
    padding: 0;
    background: none;
    border: 0;
  }
  .perspective-tile h2 button::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    border-radius: 16px;
  }
  .tile-deck {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .research-quote {
    margin: 0 0 28px;
    padding: 24px;
    background: #203d30;
    color: #fff;
    border-radius: 9px;
  }
  .research-quote blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    font: 500 21px/1.4 var(--display);
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    color: inherit;
  }
  .research-quote figcaption {
    font-size: 10px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: #d6e1d6;
    margin-top: 16px;
  }
  .research-quote a {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .card-quote {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    min-height: 210px;
  }
  .takeaways {
    background: #f1f5ef;
    border-radius: 9px;
    padding: 22px;
    margin: 10px 0 28px;
  }
  .perspective-tile h3 {
    font:
      600 11px/1.5 Inter,
      sans-serif;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  .takeaways ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 18px;
    list-style: disc;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: #40574a;
  }
  .takeaways li + li {
    margin-top: 10px;
  }
  .tile-sources {
    padding-bottom: 26px;
  }
  .tile-sources a {
    display: block;
    width: fit-content;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 8px 0;
    color: #486652;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .tile-bottom {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 20px;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 12px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .note-button {
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: none;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 550;
  }
  .note-button:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .tile-bottom button {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .tile-bottom > span {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 10px;
  }
  .manifesto {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.4fr;
    gap: 60px;
    padding: 43px 0;
    margin: 62px 0 30px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .manifesto h2 {
    font-size: 28px;
    margin-top: 13px;
  }
  .manifesto p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.9;
  }
  .manifesto a {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 16px;
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 650;
    color: #171b1d;
  }
  .manifesto a span {
    margin-left: 6px;
    font-size: 19px;
    color: #0a7e7d;
  }
  .textlink:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  dialog {
    margin: auto;
    width: min(780px, calc(100% - 32px));
    max-height: 88vh;
    overflow: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 17px;
    padding: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: #fafbf9;
  }
  dialog::backdrop {
    background: #10201899;
    backdrop-filter: blur(4px);
  }
  .dialog-bar {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    background: #fafbf9;
    padding: 18px 28px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    z-index: 1;
  }
  .dialog-bar span {
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--green);
  }
  .close {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
